        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Grease and line a 900 g (2 lb) loaf tin. Preheat the oven to 170°C (conventional)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Melt the butter, sugar, treacle, and golden syrup together in a saucepan over low heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves. Leave to cool to lukewarm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sift the flour, spices, and bicarbonate of soda into a large bowl. Beat the eggs into the cooled syrup mixture. Pour the wet ingredients into the dry and stir until smooth. Add the milk and stir again. Fold in the chopped crystallised ginger."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pour into the prepared tin. Bake at 170°C (conventional) for 55 to 65 minutes, until a skewer through the centre comes out clean and the loaf is pulling away from the sides of the tin slightly. The top should be deep brown and springy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Leave to cool in the tin for 15 minutes before turning out. The loaf is at its best the next day, when the stickiness and spice have deepened."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
